                             By:  Ulli Hernando

     This is a Telix V 3.12 Script file which allows the Telix user to send
his/her pretyped signature-file by a single key press.

     The script assumes the signature-file is called 'SIG.TXT' and that this
file is located in the Script Directory.

     The signature-file is sent by using the ASCII transfer protocol.

     Installations Instructions
     컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴컴
     1.  Place SIGNIT.SLC into the Script Directory as set by your
         configurations.
     2.  Place the signature-file 'SIG.TXT' into the Script Directory.
     3.  Change a Macro key (ALT-K) in Telix to read:  @SIGNIT
         (Often, the Function keys are used for Macros)
         Be sure to Save the changes (usually as TELIX.KEY).

     Note:  SIGNIT.SLT (the source code) is included for your convenience.
            Eg.  If you wish to alter the script (ie. change the signature
                 filename, the directory of this file, etc.).